[CENTER][SIZE=7][B]🚇 MTR-Dynmap Bridge[/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4][I]Live web map of Minecraft Transit Railway vehicles, plus MTR stations and depots on Dynmap[/I][/SIZE]

[SIZE=3][COLOR=#E53935][B]v1.0.0.3[/B][/COLOR]  •  [B]Minecraft 1.21.1 / 1.21.4[/B]  •  [B]Java 21+[/B]  •  [B]MTR 4.1.0-beta.2[/B]  •  [COLOR=#46C17A][B]Dynmap optional[/B][/COLOR][/SIZE]

[IMG]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mdreval/MTR-Dynmap-Bridge/main/docs/images/web-map-overview.jpg[/IMG]
[I]The built-in live web map — every MTR line, station and vehicle of the server in one browser tab.[/I][/CENTER]

MTR-Dynmap Bridge connects the [B]Minecraft Transit Railway (MTR 4)[/B] mod with the web. It gives your server [B]two ways[/B] to watch your transport network:
[LIST]
[*][B]🗺️ Live web map[/B] — a lightweight website built into the plugin: the real layout of your network, stations, depots and [B]smoothly moving trains, boats, cable cars and airplanes[/B]. No Dynmap required.
[*][B]📍 Dynmap markers[/B] — MTR stations and depots on your existing Dynmap.
[/LIST]
Use both together, or only one of them — each part can be switched off in [B]config.yml[/B].

[CENTER][COLOR=#E53935][B]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/B][/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B]✨ Features[/B][/SIZE]

[SIZE=4][B]🗺️ Live web map[/B] [COLOR=#E53935][I](new in 1.0.0.2)[/I][/COLOR][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Every MTR rail, [B]straight and curved[/B], in its real place — drawn [B]in the colours of your MTR lines[/B].
[*]Platforms and depot sidings marked; boat routes, cable cars and flight paths in their own style.
[*][B]Smoothly animated vehicles[/B] — trains, boats, cable cars, airplanes — in their line's colour, with the line number as a label.
[*]Stations and depots with their areas from the MTR dashboard.
[*][B]Station window:[/B] lines stopping there, vehicles at the station and vehicles heading there (distance, speed), [B]split by direction[/B], updated live.
[*][B]Lines list[/B] — both directions of a line (there and back) shown as [B]one line[/B]. Click a line to highlight it and show only its vehicles, or open it and highlight a single direction.
[*][B]Transport type switches[/B] — hide trains, boats, cable cars or airplanes with one tick.
[*]Vehicle list for the selected dimension with [B]search[/B] by line, station or destination.
[*][B]"Follow this vehicle"[/B] — the map keeps it in view.
[*]Shareable links — the page address keeps the current view.
[*][B]English / Russian[/B] interface.
[*]Optional links to your Dynmap and to MTR's own system map.
[/LIST]

