[SIZE=4][B]📍 Dynmap markers[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Automatically displays MTR stations ([B]pin[/B] icon) and depots ([B]building[/B] icon) on Dynmap.
[*]Markers of deleted stations and depots are removed automatically.
[*]Automatic MTR dimension → server world mapping, with manual overrides — no world name is hard-coded.
[*]Automatic Y coordinate restoration for stations stored without height.
[*]Configurable icons and synchronization interval.
[/LIST]

[CENTER][ATTACH=full]983207[/ATTACH]

[ATTACH]984573[/ATTACH] [ATTACH]984574[/ATTACH]
[I]MTR stations and depots on Dynmap.[/I][/CENTER]

[SIZE=4][B]⚡ Built for live servers[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]MTR data is read [B]on MTR's own simulation thread[/B], the same way MTR's own website reads it — the Minecraft server thread is never used.
[*]Rail shapes are calculated once and [B]cached[/B] until a rail changes.
[*]The website runs in separate (virtual) threads and every viewer receives [B]only what changed[/B].
[*]All reflection lookups are cached — safe on hybrid servers such as Youer.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]🛠️ Admin tools[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]/mtrmap[/B] — a clickable link to the web map for every player.
[*][B]/mtrstations[/B], [B]/mtrroutes[/B] — station and route lists in game or in the console.
[*][B]stations.txt[/B] / [B]routes.txt[/B] exports.
[*]Station and route blacklists.
[*]Old config.yml files are upgraded automatically — new settings are added with comments.
[/LIST]

[CENTER][COLOR=#E53935][B]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/B][/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B]☑️ Requirements[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Minecraft:[/B] 1.21.1 / 1.21.4.
[*][B]Server software:[/B] [B]Youer[/B] or another hybrid server that runs NeoForge mods together with the Bukkit, Spigot and Paper APIs.
[*][B]MTR:[/B] 4.1.0-beta.2 — [B]required[/B] (other MTR 4.x builds should work).
[*][B]Dynmap:[/B] [COLOR=#46C17A][B]optional[/B][/COLOR] — only needed for the Dynmap markers (3.7-beta8 tested). Without Dynmap the web map and commands keep working.
[*][B]Java:[/B] 21+ (any normal JDK/JRE).
[/LIST]

[I]Note: a plain Bukkit, Paper or Spigot server without the MTR mod has no MTR data, so there is nothing to show.[/I]

[SIZE=5][B]⬇️ Quick start[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*]Drop [B]MTR-Dynmap-Bridge-1.0.0.3.jar[/B] into the [B]plugins[/B] folder. [B]When updating, delete the old jar first[/B] (keep your config.yml).
[*]Open TCP port [B]25970[/B] in your firewall / hosting panel (or set another port in config.yml).
[*]Start the server — the console shows [B]Web map started on port 25970[/B] and then [B]MTR detected[/B].
[*]Open [B]http://<server-ip>:25970/[/B] in a browser, or type [B]/mtrmap[/B] in game.
[/LIST]
Full installation and configuration guide: see the [B]Documentation[/B] tab.

[SIZE=5][B]💻 Commands[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]/mtrmap[/B] (alias [B]/transitmap[/B]) — clickable link to the web map. Permission [B]mtrdynmap.map[/B] (everyone).
[*][B]/mtrstations [search][/B] — list of MTR stations. Permission [B]mtrdynmap.admin[/B] (op).
[*][B]/mtrroutes [search][/B] — list of MTR routes with vehicles on the way. Permission [B]mtrdynmap.admin[/B] (op).
[/LIST]

[CENTER][COLOR=#E53935][B]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/B][/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B]🚀 What's New in 1.0.0.3[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Lines with both directions[/B] — the new [B]Merge directions[/B] tick shows the two routes of a line as one line. Click it to highlight the whole line, or open it and highlight one direction (clockwise / anticlockwise for circular lines).
[*][B]Station window by direction[/B] — vehicles at the station and on their way, split by line and direction.
[*]The plugin now reads the first and last station of every route and whether it is circular.
[/LIST]

[SPOILER="Older versions"]
[B]What's New 1.0.0.2[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]Live web map[/B] built into the plugin: MTR rails with curves in the colours of your lines, platforms, depot sidings, station areas, depots and smoothly moving vehicles (trains, boats, cable cars, airplanes).
[*][B]Lines list[/B] with highlighting, [B]vehicle list[/B] with search and "follow", [B]station window[/B] with lines, vehicles at the station and vehicles heading there.
[*][B]Transport type switches[/B] — trains, boats, cable cars and airplanes can each be hidden with a tick.
[*]Data is read on [B]MTR's own simulation thread[/B] — nothing runs on the Minecraft server thread.
[*][B]Dynmap is optional[/B] — without it the web map and commands keep working. Dynmap markers are unchanged; sync interval and icons are now configurable.
[*][B]English / Russian[/B] localization of the website and messages ([B]language: "en"[/B] or [B]"ru"[/B]).
[*]New commands [B]/mtrmap[/B], [B]/mtrstations[/B], [B]/mtrroutes[/B]; stations.txt / routes.txt exports; station and route blacklists.
[*]Existing config.yml files get the new settings appended automatically; worlds mappings are kept.
[*]Quieter console.
[/LIST]

[B]What's New 1.0.0.1[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Fixed Dynmap markers remaining after MTR stations or depots were removed; automatic cleanup of station and depot markers.
[*]Automatic world and dimension detection, with optional world mappings in config.yml.
[*]Automatic Y coordinate restoration when determining the surface location.
[/LIST]

[B]What's New 1.0.0.0[/B]
[LIST]
[*]First release: MTR stations and depots on Dynmap.
[/LIST]
[/SPOILER]

